    "The four current sources implement the declared fixed-normal-checkpoint missing49 workflow. No source correction remains required by this review.",
    "The local continuation waits for the existing expert-seed queue final normal GT/raw/CPU status. That producer emits this status only after original three-dataset normal closure, the original RGBNT100 CPU intake, seeds43/44 native/full50 closures, archive verification and normal seed analysis. No missing NN is launched during this wait.",
    "The job registry includes both I42 controls on all three datasets and only a separately normal-selected RGBNT201 winner when its seed is43/44. Normal Best-of3 is computed from six complete normal runs in seed42/43/44 order, and per-run epochs are first maximum-mAP epoch in ordered epoch1..50 tables. No missing condition selects a seed or epoch. At most two supplements are added, with no duplicate seed42 run.",
    "The wrapper delegates seed42 to the existing three-dataset builder and seeds43/44 only on RGBNT201 to the fixed-DeMo42 expert builder. The selected model loads best.pth strictly; the evaluator retains unchanged four-state inference and selected normal feature/distance exactness checks. These are inference paths, with no optimizer updates, loss changes or new trained weights.",
    "The two controller lanes bind frequency to physicalGPU2 and axis to physicalGPU3 and serialize each lane. All declared checkpoints first complete the seven small availability checks plus full-normal four-state installed-GT audit and raw archival. Full49 requires the complete native result; final raw/state counts are49N/196N for N=6..8.",
    "Independent installed-GT recount preserves same-ID/same-camera exclusion for RGBNT and same-ID/same-scene exclusion for MSVR310, checking six metrics, CMC50, per-query rows and identity/camera/scene groups. RAW_READY follows this audit. Local size/SHA verification occurs before the ACK that permits remote raw unlink; each evaluator holds only one live raw condition.",
    "The deployment uses existing local normal-array receipts, restores only selected normal arrays and checks local D headroom plus remote restore bytes+1.6GB. The existing G100 relocation receipt is consumed without moving or replaying historical data. After both inference phases, native raw is retired only when the corresponding full raw receipt and both actual local file size/SHA checks match. Restored normal copies are removed only after all NN is closed; selected best.pth and unique local normal/full raw are preserved.",
    "The reducer paths and fields match the six actual historical G full49 outputs and three original DeMo audit outputs. It reads these CPU text artifacts and creates no historical NN replay. The primary I42 comparisons include own00/10/01, matched ordinary-frequency control, corresponding G and original DeMo. Separately selected RGBNT201 axis and frequency winners each include own00/10/01, corresponding G and original comparisons; selected-winner and I42 comparisons are explicitly seed-labelled.",
    "Paired metadata, valid-query counts, scalar six metrics, CMC50 and identity/camera/scene groups are checked before differences. Rank1 rescue-minus-harm is checked against the metric delta. Availability groups retain49/7/30/12/6/6/36 conditions, with AP improvement/harm counts and paired-query exports. The report discloses benchmark selection, original50 versus two-stage100 budgets, fixed-teacher conditional repeats, repeated-query dependence, mixed-source ordinary control and the disjoint private-coordinate limitation."
